title touchstone — the loop that has to get better

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  READ THIS FIRST — three conventions, then what this redraw changed.
//
//  1 · WHERE A NODE CARRIES A PHASE COLOUR, THAT COLOUR IS THE SCHEDULE.
//      A node coloured for a phase it is not in is the quiet lie the key exists
//      to stop. The schedule is most of the risk, so that is the colour that has
//      to be right.
//      ⛔ THE RULE IS ABOUT THE SCHEDULE COLOURS ALONE. red, purple and grey have
//         their own legend rows and are not phase claims. Nodes with NO colour
//         carry their phase in the label as Pn.n, which is the real mechanism.
//      ⛔ A CENSUS OF COLOURS WRITTEN INTO PROSE GOES STALE ON THE NEXT EDIT.
//         Re-derive it from the DSL; never step it by hand. Command in
//         diagrams/README.md. The previous header carried three such counts and
//         all three were wrong within an hour of being written.
//      ✅ GREEN MEANS TWO THINGS — "phase 0, shipped" OR "a good outcome" — and
//         the KEY SAYS SO (D-053). It applies to GREEN ALONE. Any other colour
//         acquiring a second meaning is DEF-013 recurring, and the giveaway is
//         that the key will not mention it.
//
//  2 · THE BOXES CARRY THE NAME AND THE RULE. THESE COMMENTS CARRY THE ARGUMENT.
//      ⛔ ONE line a node. TWO at the outside. If it needs a paragraph it is an
//         argument, and arguments live down here, where they cost no pixels.
//
//  3 · EVERY NODE NAMING A file.py:LINE MUST RESOLVE, IN EXACTLY ONE FILE, IN AN
//      APPROVED REPO — touchstone, or tau2-bench — tau2 at commit a2c024725189 (MIT). D-068.
//      ⛔ AMBIGUITY IS A FAILURE, NOT A NEAR MISS. tau2 has SIX files called
//         environment.py; the first draft of this diagram named the BARE file with
//         the line number, and the guard resolved it to retail's 54-line domain file
//         and reported a line past EOF. The line number was right. The NAME was
//         ambiguous. ⛔ AND THE BARE NAME IS NOT WRITTEN OUT HERE EITHER, not even
//         as a quotation — the guard cannot tell a citation from a claim, and a rule
//         whose own explanation trips it is a rule that gets switched off.
//         scripts/check-diagram-nodes.sh is what caught it and it fails on
//         ambiguity now rather than taking the first hit.
//      ⚠ AND THE GUARD'S APPROVED ROOT IS NARROWER THAN D-068's. It resolves inside
//         src/tau2 only, so the retail POLICY file — which lives under data/ — does
//         not resolve there. Section 8b names it in prose rather than as a path,
//         because loosening a guard to make a label pass is the wrong direction.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  WHAT THIS REDRAW CHANGED — D-068, and it is a redraw rather than an amendment.
//
//  D-062 replaced the specimen: infra-RCA out, τ²-bench retail in. D-066 archived
//  the old one whole to `incident-specimen` at 109c424 before a file left main.
//  Sections 1–4 of the previous picture — the corpus, the graph, the state keys,
//  the tools — were ALL specimen. They are gone from here because they are gone
//  from main, not because they were wrong.
//
//  ⚠ THE STALENESS SPLIT THAT MADE THIS SAFE TO DO. Two kinds of node named a
//  file that is not on disk, and they need OPPOSITE treatment:
//    · 7 named files that were ARCHIVED — domain.py, incidents/generate.py,
//      incidents/renderers.py, suite/benchmark/truth.json, manifest.json,
//      suite/CHANGELOG.md, tests/unit/test_invariants.py. Confirmed present on
//      `incident-specimen` with git ls-tree. Those are WRONG and they are cut.
//    · 12+ named files that were NEVER BUILT ANYWHERE — loop/*.py, gate/*.py.
//      Those are CORRECT. D-021 draws before code, so a diagram naming an unbuilt
//      file is the gate working as designed.
//  ⛔ A naive "does this file exist" check condemns the entire planned
//     architecture. The test is `git ls-tree incident-specimen`, never `ls`.
//
//  ⚠ AND THE DECISIVE DEFECT WAS ABSENCE, NOT STALENESS. Nothing from D-062
//    through D-067 appeared anywhere in the old picture. A diagram that is
//    merely out of date still argues for something; one that is silent about
//    the last six decisions argues for nothing.
//
//  🔴 AND IT HAPPENED AGAIN, ON THIS FILE, WITHIN TWO DAYS. On 2026-08-21 D-071
//    through D-079 — NINE decisions — appeared in zero labels and zero comments
//    here, while scripts/check-diagram.py returned PASS at 228 citations. The
//    warning three paragraphs above was written about the LAST redraw and did
//    not prevent the next one, because a paragraph is not an instrument.
//    Milestone 10 is now that instrument: it reads DECISIONS.md, takes every
//    decision at or above a hand-set watermark (D-068, the redraw that produced
//    this picture) and fails on any that is drawn nowhere. Two are exempt as
//    non-structural and each carries its reason in the script. Both failure
//    branches were negative-tested before the milestone was believed.
//    ⛔ RAISING THE WATERMARK IS A CLAIM THAT A REDRAW READ EVERYTHING BELOW IT.
//       It is not a way to make the milestone quiet.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE ONE STRUCTURAL FIND, AND IT IS WHY PHASE 1 IS SMALL.
//
//  tau2.utils.llm_utils.generate() at llm_utils.py:355 is the SINGLE chokepoint
//  for EVERY model role in τ². The agent (llm_agent.py:128), the user simulator
//  (user_simulator.py:235) and the hallucination reviewer (hallucination_reviewer.py:196)
//  all import that one function. So the integration is ONE adapter dispatching on
//  the `model` argument — not four.
//
//  litellm is displaced there, and that has a consequence D-063 did not survive:
//  D-063 put the traces on litellm's OTel callback. litellm leaves the agent path
//  at P1.1, so that callback sees NOTHING. touchstone emits its own spans or it
//  has none. The grey LiteLLM box and the TelemetryPy edges are that change, said
//  in the picture rather than buried in a decision file.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE THREE DECISIONS — the reason the word "promotion" is gone.
//
//  The old picture had one gate: compare.py, five conditions, PROMOTE or REFUSE.
//  That collapsed three different decisions into one word, and the word named the
//  least interesting of them:
//
//    1 · refuse a TOOL CALL          runtime, at make_tool_call()   — P3.1
//    2 · reject a CANDIDATE VERSION  at compare                     — P2.4
//    3 · admit a MINED CASE          at suite admit                 — P3.5
//
//  ⛔ ALL THREE ARE MECHANICAL. ANYTHING WITH A MODEL IN IT CANNOT GATE. That is
//  the invariant this whole picture is arranged around, and it is why every node
//  in the D1/D2/D3 column is green-on-dark rather than amber. D-064 says where the
//  model IS allowed to sit: TRANSLATION — turn a stated constraint into a
//  predicate — never VERDICT.
//
//  ⚠ DECISION 3 WAS DRAWN IN GREY FOR FOUR PASSES WITH NO BUILD ROW, AND IT HAS
//  ONE NOW (D-070). D-030 cut mining as the largest single cut; what it cut turned
//  out to be the INNER LOOP — section 8b, the one stage here that makes the
//  measurement bigger instead of reporting it. It stayed drawn throughout, because
//  the failure this project has already had once is a mechanism specified in full
//  and built by no row (DEF-009) — which is exactly why it was still findable.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  WHY THE SCORER STAYS HONEST, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED.
//
//  τ²'s COMPOSITE retail reward is NOT mechanical, and the gate is a component of
//  it rather than the whole. reward_breakdown["DB"] is a database-state diff
//  against an annotated goal, written as its own key by evaluator_env.py:153 on
//  every task. THAT is what gates. The composite is reported beside it. D-069.
//  ⚠ I GOT THIS WRONG THREE TIMES and the third is the one worth the ink:
//    (1) "the scorer has no LLM judge" — it has an NL-assertion path, LLM-graded.
//    (2) "the NL evaluator is in the reward path, 112 of 114 tasks" — read off
//        reward_basis. CORRECT, and I then talked myself out of it.
//    (3) "reward_breakdown is the execution record and never contains one" —
//        measured over 1,824 shipped sims, true of THOSE sims, and about a task
//        set no run will ever load again. The leaderboard runs used the original
//        τ-bench basis; tasks.json was rewritten under them. TWO FILES, ONE
//        CHECKOUT, FOUR-DIGIT n ON THE STALE ONE.
//  ⛔ THE COMPONENT IS NOT FREE. DB-only and full reward disagreed on 6, 16, 12
//     and 29 of 456 simulations across the four baselines — 1.3% to 6.4%. That was
//     DB vs DB×COMMUNICATE; today's comparison is DB vs DB×NL_ASSERTION, so the
//     number is an order of magnitude, NOT a transferable rate. Gating on a
//     component is a DIFFERENT measurement, not a simpler one, and P1.7 measures
//     the joint distribution before any gate is built on it.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE FIVE MODEL PINS, AND THE CONSTRAINT THAT SET THEM.
//
//  ⛔ ANTHROPIC ONLY. ollama and Cerebras are reachable from this machine and both
//  stay `doctor` diagnostics — never model sources. D-067 third amendment.
//  ⚠ THIS BLOCK USED TO SAY THE README CONTRADICTED IT, AND THE README WAS FIXED
//  FIRST. So for a while the DIAGRAM was the stale document, asserting a defect in
//  a file that no longer had one — and it said so in a RENDERED LABEL, not just
//  down here. A pointer at another file's error is a claim with a shelf life, and
//  nothing sweeps backwards from the fix to the pointer (rule 22).
//
//  The deciding constraint is QUOTA SHAPE, not price. Measured off the SDK's
//  RateLimitEvent: rate_limit_type='five_hour', overage_status='rejected',
//  overage_disabled_reason='org_level_disabled'. The cap REJECTS rather than
//  bills, so exhausting it does not cost money — it kills a run in flight. Opus as
//  the agent was the realistic choice and lost to exactly that.
//
//  ⚠ AND THE FIRST PROBE REPORTED ALL FOUR CLAUDE MODELS AS FAIL. The probe's
//  result capture was broken, not the models — is_error=False, cost $0.0432 on the
//  same calls. A NEGATIVE RESULT FROM A PROBE YOU JUST WROTE IS A CLAIM ABOUT THE
//  PROBE FIRST. It nearly removed the whole Claude 5 family from consideration.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

direction down
colorMode pastel
styleMode shadow
typeface clean

legend [position: top-left] {
  [color: green, label: "phase 0 — shipped, or a good outcome"]
  [color: blue, label: "phase 1 — next"]
  [color: orange, label: "phase 2 — v0.1.0"]
  [color: pink, label: "phase 3 — v0.2.0"]
  [color: grey, label: "deferred, cut, or displaced"]
  [color: red, label: "an invariant, or a never"]
  [color: purple, label: "an OPEN QUESTION — nobody has decided yet"]
  [connection: -->, label: "reads it — does not trigger it"]
}

// ── 1 · the specimen. External, pinned, and NOT OURS — which is the whole point of D-062.
Tau2 [color: grey, icon: package, label: "1 · τ²-bench retail — EXTERNAL · MIT · commit a2c024725189 · 257 of 257 blobs verified against upstream\nnot written here, not vendored here — 114 tasks stay upstream · the string 1.0.1 names TWO trees (DEF-055)"] {
  Orch [icon: repeat, label: "orchestrator.py:260 — Orchestrator.run\ndrives one simulation to its end"]
  AgentTurn [color: orange, icon: cpu, label: "llm_agent.py:128 — the agent under test\nTHE THING BEING MEASURED"]
  UserSim [color: orange, icon: user, label: "user_simulator.py:235 — the customer\nFROZEN APPARATUS (D-067)"]
  Reviewer [color: orange, icon: search, label: "hallucination_reviewer.py:196 — opt-in\nvalidates the SIMULATOR, not the agent"]
  Gen [color: red, icon: git-merge, label: "llm_utils.py:355 — generate()\nTHE SINGLE SEAM · all four roles import it"]
  LiteLLM [color: grey, icon: slash, label: "llm_utils.py:15 — litellm.completion\nDISPLACED at P1.1 — and its OTel callback goes with it"]
  EnvCall [color: red, icon: shield, label: "environment/environment.py:158 — make_tool_call()\nTHE ENFORCEMENT POINT · every tool execution passes here"]
  Mutates [icon: edit-3, label: "environment/environment.py:130 — _is_mutating_tool()\nτ² already split read from write — do not re-derive it"]
  Eval [icon: check-square, label: "evaluator.py:88 — evaluate_simulation\nruns AFTER the simulation, never during it"]
  Reward [color: red, icon: award, label: "reward_breakdown[DB] — the gating number\nNO MODEL · composite reported beside it, never gated · D-069"]
}

Orch > AgentTurn
Orch > UserSim
Orch > Reviewer: opt-in — --auto-review
AgentTurn > Gen
UserSim > Gen
Reviewer > Gen
AgentTurn > EnvCall: every tool the agent calls
EnvCall > Mutates: read or write?
Orch > Eval > Reward

// ── 2 · the seam, and the pins behind it.
Seam [color: blue, icon: git-merge, label: "2 · the seam — P1.1"] {
  Adapter [color: blue, icon: link, label: "adapter.py — P1.1\nthe Claude Agent SDK behind generate(), dispatching on `model`\nONE adapter, FOUR roles — because there is one chokepoint"]
  Sdk [color: orange, icon: cpu, label: "ClaudeSDKClient — claude_agent_sdk\nsetting_sources=[] — the EMPTY LIST, never None (D-034)"]
  Anthropic [shape: cylinder, color: orange, icon: cloud, label: "Anthropic — subscription auth, NOT an API key\nfive-hour window · the cap REJECTS, it does not bill"]
}

Cfg [color: green, icon: settings, label: "config.py — P0 ✅ shipped · FIVE model pins (D-067)\nMODEL · USER_MODEL · JUDGE_MODEL · NL_ASSERTION_MODEL · REVIEW_MODEL"]
NoOther [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-octagon, label: "ANTHROPIC ONLY — ollama and Cerebras are `doctor` diagnostics\nNEVER model sources · the quota REJECTS, so a wrong pin kills a run (D-067)"]

Gen > Adapter: REPLACED at the seam
Gen --> LiteLLM: what it used to call
Adapter > Sdk > Anthropic
Cfg > Adapter: which pin, per role
NoOther --> Cfg
Doctor [color: green, icon: activity, label: "doctor.py — P0, THE FIRST FILE WRITTEN\n✅ shipped: `touchstone doctor` runs today · probes the AGENT pin by live call\nP1.0 adds the τ² data check · it checks NO trace server, because there is not one (D-077)"]
Doctor > Cfg

// ── 3 · the gates. Shadow earns enforce; nothing here carries a model in its verdict.
Gates3 [color: orange, icon: filter, label: "3 · the gates — D-064 · D-065\na gate is an EXTRACTED CONSTRAINT plus a MECHANICAL CHECK"] {
  Tier1 [color: orange, icon: hash, label: "gate/tier1.py — P2.1 · FIVE DB constraints, NO model\nmeasured: 0/408 passing sessions violated, 1/48 failing ones did"]
  Tier2 [color: orange, icon: cpu, label: "gate/extract.py — P2.2 · the model TRANSLATES a stated constraint\ninto a predicate. The VERDICT is mechanical. It never judges 'did well'"]
  Shadow [color: orange, icon: eye, label: "SHADOW — P2.3 · judges a COMPLETED session, acts on nothing\na gate earns enforcement here, or it does not get it"]
  Enforce [color: pink, icon: shield, label: "gate/enforce.py — P3.1 · REFUSES the call before it executes\nthe hook at make_tool_call()"]
}

Tier1 > Shadow
Tier2 > Shadow
Shadow > Enforce: ONLY with a measured precision and recall (D-065)
Enforce > EnvCall: refuse — before the write happens
Precision [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "PERFECT PRECISION, 2.1% RECALL on a strong agent\nthe low recall is the FEATURE — only a gate that never fires falsely can be enforced"]
Precision --> Tier1
Headroom [shape: document, color: orange, icon: target, label: "tier 2 targets the 26 FLAKY tasks — where the headroom is\n⚠ its false-positive rate on the 85 always-passing tasks is what shadow measures"]
Headroom --> Tier2

// ── 4 · what an attempt lands on. One status, plus an orthogonal flag.
Ends [color: red, icon: flag, label: "4 · exactly ONE status per attempt — docs/09 §6"] {
  Scored [color: green, icon: check-circle, label: "scored — counts toward everything"]
  ParseFail [color: red, icon: x-circle, label: "parse_failure — scored WRONG\nnever retried (D-013)"]
  Voided [color: grey, icon: slash, label: "void — rate limit, or model changed\ncounts toward NOTHING (D-015)"]
  Incomplete [color: grey, icon: pause-circle, label: "incomplete — process died\nthe five-hour window is the realistic cause"]
}
Orch > Ends: every attempt lands on exactly one
BudgetFlag [shape: document, color: red, icon: dollar-sign, label: "budget_exceeded — a FLAG, never a status\nlands BESIDE any of the four, NEVER instead of one"]
Orch > BudgetFlag: orthogonal to where the attempt lands

// ── 5 · telemetry. This is the edge D-063 got wrong, and the picture says so.
TelemetryPy [color: blue, icon: activity, label: "5 · telemetry.py — P1.2\ntouchstone.* — NEVER gen_ai.* (D-017)\n🆕 the span is opened by adapter.py ITSELF (D-073) — no instrumentor can emit it"]
D063 [shape: document, color: purple, icon: help-circle, label: "D-063 assumed litellm's OTel callback\nP1.1 kills that assumption — this is a CHANGE to a recorded decision"]
D063 --> TelemetryPy
Adapter > TelemetryPy: one span per model call, all four roles
EnvCall > TelemetryPy: one span per tool call, and per REFUSAL
Reward > TelemetryPy: the label, joined at end-of-simulation on session_id

Stores [color: blue, icon: hard-drive, label: "6 · what survives the process"] {
  Spans [shape: cylinder, icon: file-text, label: "results/spans/(version).jsonl\nthe scorer's ONLY input"]
  Bench [shape: document, color: blue, icon: lock, label: "suite/benchmark/ — P1.3 · task IDS and a hash\nNEVER task bytes — vendoring makes us the corpus's owner again"]
}
TelemetryPy > Spans
Bench > Orch: which tasks — the ids only

// ── 7 · the driver and the scorer.
CliPy [color: blue, icon: terminal, label: "cli.py — P0 shipped `doctor`\nP1.6 adds run · score · suite"]
RunPy [color: blue, icon: play, label: "loop/run.py — k attempts, config.K = 3 (D-030)\n--resume · attempt cache (D-015)"]
CliPy > Doctor: the P0 subcommand, and the only one that runs today
CliPy > RunPy > Orch

Scoring [color: blue, icon: bar-chart-2, label: "7 · scoring — P1.5"] {
  ScorePy [color: blue, icon: bar-chart-2, label: "loop/score.py — NO model call (D-007)\nspans + reward_breakdown → results/(version).json\npass^k is the HEADLINE · pass@1 beside it — BOTH, especially when they differ"]
  Diag [shape: document, color: red, icon: eye-off, label: "diagnostics{} — inside results/(version).json\ncompare.py NEVER reads inside it — ONE TEST proves it (D-045)\nNO OUTGOING EDGE, ON PURPOSE"]
  Judge [color: orange, icon: award, label: "the rubric judge — JUDGE_MODEL, cheapest tier on purpose\nit CANNOT GATE — that is why it is allowed to exist at all"]
}
Spans > ScorePy
Reward > ScorePy: the answer key, and it is τ²'s, not ours
ScorePy > Diag: the OTHER output — and it stops here
Judge > Diag: writes the rubric fields — and reaches NOTHING else
DeepEval [color: grey, icon: bar-chart-2, label: "deepeval — an OPTIONAL extra, `diagnostics` · D-076\nnothing that gates may import it · telemetry opted out at import"]
DeepEval > Diag: trajectory diagnostics — and, like the judge, reaches NOTHING else
Shadow --> Diag: the shadow scores land here until a gate earns enforcement

// ── 8 · decision 2. Five conditions, all mechanical.
Cmp [color: grey, icon: filter, label: "8 · loop/compare.py — P2.4 · DEFERRED, D-080 · NOTHING HERE RUNS\nspecified in full because this is what it revives to — it has no SECOND OPERAND until a second version exists"] {
  C1 [icon: hash, label: "1 · benchmark_hash(C) == benchmark_hash(I)"]
  C2 [color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "2 · NO per-task regression — THE ONE THAT WORKS\nfires on pass^k → not-pass^k ONLY (D-008)"]
  C3 [icon: trending-up, label: "3 · strict improvement on ≥ 1 metric\nelse a no-op is accepted"]
  C4 [icon: dollar-sign, label: "4 · no budget breach — cost per success, p95"]
  C5 [color: grey, icon: lock, label: "5 · no locked task fails — ONE-WAY\nopen/locked is DELETED, not vacuous — it locks on an ACCEPTED version and there are none (D-080)"]
}
C1 > C2 > C3 > C4 > C5
ScorePy > Cmp: results/(version).json — the scored half only
Accepted [shape: oval, color: green, icon: check, label: "ACCEPT — vN is the champion"]
Refused [shape: oval, color: red, icon: x, label: "REJECT — the rejection IS the result\nNEVER fixed by weakening the baseline"]
C5 > Accepted: all five hold
Cmp > Refused: any ONE fails

// ── 8a · THE FEED (D-080). The inner loop needed a failing trace and a control set, and
//  that was the ONLY thing the outer loop owed it — so it is fed from τ²'s own shipped runs
//  instead. ⚠ SELECTION IS NOT GATING, and reusing one number for both was the defect.
//  reward_breakdown[DB] compares FINAL DATABASE STATE and is blind to how the state was
//  reached: an agent that skips a required confirmation and still writes the correct row
//  scores DB == 1. Feeding on DB == 0 alone left 371 such traces in the SILENCE SET, where
//  a CORRECT predicate would have been rejected as a false positive.
Feed [color: pink, icon: filter, label: "8a · the feed — D-080 · τ²'s OWN shipped runs, never a run of ours"] {
  Corpus [color: grey, icon: archive, label: "1,712 simulations τ²-bench SHIPS — data/tau2/results/final/\n107 of 114 tasks — the 7 whose gold actions moved are EXCLUDED, not repaired"]
  Select [shape: diamond, color: pink, icon: git-merge, label: "select — the UNION of THREE signals\n⚠ NOT reward_breakdown[DB] == 0 alone"]
  Anom [color: orange, icon: alert-circle, label: "834 ANOMALOUS\n407 the DB check failed · +371 DB PASSED and an action_check failed · +56 a WRITE nobody confirmed"]
  Clean [color: green, icon: check-circle, label: "878 CLEAN — none of the three signals\nTHE SILENCE SET · a gate that fires here is a FALSE POSITIVE"]
}
Corpus > Select
Select > Anom
Select > Clean
SelNotGate [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "SELECTION IS NOT GATING — D-080\nDB stays the GATE's metric because it is mechanical, and it is a POOR SELECTOR for the same reason — it cannot see process\n⚠ the 56 is an UPPER BOUND from a regex over the last user message before each WRITE — enough to widen the selector, NOT a figure to quote"]
SelNotGate --> Select

// ── 8b · THE INNER LOOP (D-070). Every other stage on this page runs ONCE per
//  candidate version. This one runs up to n times on a SINGLE failing trace, and it
//  is the only mechanism here that makes the measurement grow rather than report it.
//  The model sits in TRANSLATE and nowhere else — the verdict at TEST is a predicate
//  evaluation, which is the invariant of section 9 applied to the loop that feeds it.
//  ⚠ THE SCOPE FILTER USED TO STAND HERE AND IT IS DELETED — D-081, DEF-056. A diamond
//  asked "does this break a rule someone WROTE DOWN?" and routed a `no` to a second
//  terminal. It was called MECHANICAL in docs/02-gates.md and it named no file, no
//  predicate and no model. ⛔ IT COULD NOT HAVE BEEN MECHANICAL: a mechanical answer to
//  "was a stated rule broken?" IS the predicate translate produces, so the filter wanted
//  the loop's output as its own input. run_predicate() was always the only filter that
//  defended anything — a candidate that fires on the clean set is rejected whatever a
//  scope check believed. ⚠ WHAT IT COST TO DELETE: up to n model calls on a trace with no
//  rule to find. Unpaid today, and the exhaustion records ARE the measurement of it.
//  ⚠ The phase-3 exit gate still requires one recorded UNMINEABLE and now gets a BETTER
//  one — five attempts and five counterexamples, not a bare assertion that no rule
//  existed.
Mine [color: pink, icon: refresh-cw, label: "8b · mine — P3.4 · THE INNER LOOP, and a second LangGraph graph (D-071) · up to n = 5 attempts on ONE failing trace\nONE decision point, and it holds no model — the scope filter is DELETED (D-081) · the outer loop REPORTS a number; this loop makes the number COVER MORE"] {
  M0 [color: pink, icon: alert-circle, label: "analyst · one ANOMALOUS session, drawn from the 834 — D-080\nevery signal computed by τ²'s own evaluator, before we looked at it"]
  MT [color: orange, icon: cpu, label: "1 · author — TRANSLATE — a model turns that stated rule into a predicate\nD-064 · it proposes a CANDIDATE, it never decides"]
  MCrit [color: orange, icon: eye, label: "2 · critic — reads the candidate BEFORE it is run · D-071\nit exists because D-040 admitted the hole: a rule can be reproducible,\ndistinct, non-void and still measure something uninteresting"]
  MTest [shape: diamond, color: orange, icon: check-square, label: "3 · run_predicate() — mechanical, no model, and this IS the whole verdict\nfires on the TARGET session? must be YES\nfires on ANY of the 878 CLEAN? must be NO"]
  MGive [shape: oval, color: grey, icon: x-circle, label: "after n attempts · UNMINEABLE\nevery attempt and its counterexample recorded\n⚠ a RESULT, not an error — and not retried forever"]
}
M0 > MT: straight to the author — there is no pre-check, and never was one that worked
MT > MCrit > MTest
MTest > MT: either fails — hand back the COUNTEREXAMPLE, attempt i+1 sees what i got wrong
MTest > MGive: attempt n
Anom > M0: one anomalous trace at a time
Clean > MTest: the silence set — the NO half of the verdict
Overfit [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-triangle, label: "SILENT ON THE PASSING SET IS A CLAIM ABOUT THE SESSIONS THAT RAN\nnever about the domain — and the SLOWER CONTROL that used to cover it is GONE\n⚠ a case arrived `open` and gated only once an ACCEPTED version was quiet on it — D-080 deleted that, so an admitted predicate rests ENTIRELY on this corpus"]
Overfit --> MTest

// ── 8c · THE CURATOR'S TWO MEMORIES (D-078), and the first thing to say is which memory
//  this is NOT. It is not the agent's. The agent's memory is FROZEN and reset per attempt,
//  because it is the thing being measured; this one GROWS, because it is loop plumbing.
//  ⛔ NEITHER IS A MEMORY LIBRARY, A VECTOR STORE, OR CONVERSATION HISTORY. D-022 and D-027
//     are unchanged and this decision does not reopen them.
//  ⚠ THE ASYMMETRY IS THE DESIGN. Positive memory is EXACT because a predicate either fires
//    or it does not — you query it by running it, so it cannot drift from what it claims.
//    Negative memory is a HEURISTIC view and says so: Igor (CCS'21) measured stack-hash
//    bucketing over-counting distinct crashes by 1–2 orders of magnitude and under-counting
//    coverage by 2–3. A negative signature is the same shape of guess, so it is DERIVED and
//    never stored — a `sig_version` bump rebuilds every bucket rather than migrating it.
Curator [color: pink, icon: database, label: "8c · the curator's TWO memories — P3.4 · D-078\nNOT the agent's memory — that one is FROZEN and reset per attempt, because it is what is measured"] {
  PosMem [color: green, icon: check-square, label: "positive — THE ACTIVE RULE SET, queried by RUNNING it\nexact, because a predicate either fires or it does not"]
  NegMem [color: grey, icon: x-square, label: "negative — a RECOMPUTABLE VIEW over retained failing traces\nheuristic, derived-never-stored · a sig_version bump rebuilds it, never migrates it"]
}
Admit --> PosMem: an admitted rule IS the positive memory
MGive --> NegMem: every UNMINEABLE lands here, with its counterexamples
NegMem --> M0: has this shape already been dealt with? — prevalence ranking, D-078 · D-081 rewired this from the deleted filter

// ── 8d · WITHDRAWN 2026-08-21, AND THE WITHDRAWAL IS THE ENTRY. A `Human` node stood here
//  for one day carrying "D-079 part 3 · the HUMAN REMEDY", with edges from MSkip and Refused.
//  ⛔ IT WAS NEVER DECIDED. On 2026-08-20 the instruction was "I have suggested to change only
//     human in loop (discard it)", and on 2026-08-21 the follow-up was "I never said" about the
//     gate-blocks-and-a-human-fixes-it framing being attributed back. The one supporting remark —
//     "some human will definetly update the prompt/policy/rules" — was made inside a hypothesis
//     prefaced "This is just an thought, we aren't planning to run retail agents."
//  🔴 THE MECHANISM IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING. A correction arrived naming TWO things; one half
//     was applied and the other half was not re-derived. That is rule 10 — a correction is the
//     highest-error, lowest-re-reading edit in the file — and it produced a NODE, not a sentence.
//  ⛔ A REMARK INSIDE A HYPOTHESIS THE SPEAKER HAS ALREADY DISCLAIMED IS NOT A DECISION.
//     Grade it U, or do not draw it. An invented reason collapses on "what else did you consider?"
//  ✅ WHAT SURVIVES D-079 is below, and it is the half nobody disputed: evals are the forcing
//     function, and the STANDARD they measure against does not move. MGive is a plain
//     terminal now — it RECORDS, which is all the phase-3 exit gate ever asked of it. (MSkip stood
//     beside it until D-081 deleted the scope filter; MGive is the only terminal left.)
Immutable [shape: document, color: red, icon: lock, label: "THE STANDARD DOES NOT MOVE — D-079\nthe retail policy document is ground truth the gate derives from · the agent's prompt, rules and tools are the lever\na gate made green by editing the standard is 'the test failed so I changed the test'"]
Immutable --> MT

// ── 9 · the three decisions, side by side. None of them may contain a model.
Decisions [color: red, icon: git-branch, label: "9 · THREE decisions — and 'promotion' named only the middle one"] {
  D1 [icon: shield, label: "1 · refuse a TOOL CALL — runtime, P3.1\nno model in the verdict"]
  D2 [icon: filter, label: "2 · reject a CANDIDATE VERSION — at compare, P2.4\nno model in the verdict"]
  D3 [icon: filter, label: "3 · admit a MINED CASE — at suite admit, P3.5\nno model in the verdict · fed by the inner loop, section 8b"]
}
Enforce > D1
Cmp > D2
Invariant [shape: document, color: red, icon: alert-octagon, label: "ANYTHING THAT GATES IS MECHANICAL\nANYTHING WITH A MODEL IN IT CANNOT GATE\nD-064 puts the model in TRANSLATION, never in the VERDICT"]
Invariant --> Decisions

Admit [color: green, icon: filter, label: "10 · the five admission gates — P3.5, all mechanical, no human is a step"] {
  A1 [icon: repeat, label: "1 · reproducible"]
  A2 [icon: activity, label: "2 · not_flaky"]
  A3 [icon: slash, label: "3 · not_a_void"]
  A4 [icon: git-branch, label: "4 · distinct"]
  A5 [icon: edit, label: "5 · justified — a `why` is REQUIRED"]
}
A1 > A2 > A3 > A4 > A5
A5 > D3
MTest --> Admit: both hold — the predicate goes to the five gates
Admit --> C5: the ONLY thing condition 5 would read

