// ── 13 · the gate on the gates.
DiagGate [shape: diamond, color: red, icon: alert-octagon, label: "STEP 0 OF EVERY PHASE — D-021, docs/07\nthe diagram, approved and committed BEFORE the first line of implementation\napproval is EXPLICIT — silence is not approval (docs/07 §6)"]
PhaseGates [icon: check-square, label: "13 · the four phase exit gates"] {
  P0Gate [color: green, icon: check-circle, label: "phase 0 exit — ✅ PASSED\nD-001 carries the live `touchstone doctor` output, verbatim"]
  P1Gate [color: blue, icon: check-square, label: "phase 1 exit — the strongest gate here\nscore v1 TWICE from committed spans → byte-identical results/v1.json\nreward_breakdown carries a DB key on EVERY scored simulation — that key is what gates"]
  P2Gate [color: orange, icon: alert-triangle, label: "phase 2 exit — every gate carries a SHADOW score\na gate with no shadow number does not reach phase 3"]
  P3Gate [color: pink, icon: x-circle, label: "phase 3 exit — a REFUSED tool call is in a committed trace\none candidate is rejected · ONE trace mined end to end · ONE recorded UNMINEABLE"]
}
DiagGate > PhaseGates: blocks the START of every phase — the other four block the end
P0Gate > P1Gate > P2Gate > P3Gate
NegControl --> P2Gate: the proof the gate can reject
Doctor --> P0Gate: its verbatim output IS D-001
Enforce --> P3Gate: a refusal that was SEEN, not one that was wired
MGive --> P3Gate: the loop is only tested when it has been seen to GIVE UP

// ── 14 · the guards.
Guards [color: grey, icon: shield, label: "14 · scripts/ — the tooling that checks the WORK · NAMED BY NO PHASE\n⚠ TWO OF THE THREE ARE DELIBERATELY UNTRACKED — this label said COMMITTED until 2026-08-21"] {
  CheckDiag [color: red, icon: image, label: "check-diagram.py — the D-021 guard, TEN milestones · local, not tracked\nit reads DECISIONS.md and DEFECTS.md, which are gitignored — published it would resolve nothing\nthe only check that reads the RENDER, not the source"]
  CheckNodes [color: red, icon: crosshair, label: "check-diagram-nodes.sh — D-068 · local, not tracked\nevery path-and-line node resolves\nAMBIGUITY FAILS — tau2 has six files of one name"]
  CheckLinks [icon: link, label: "check-links.py — the ONE that is committed\nevery markdown link resolves\n⚠ against GIT, never the working tree"]
}
CheckDiag > DiagGate: the evidence D-021 asks for
CheckNodes > DiagGate: and the evidence that each name points somewhere real
CheckLinks --> PhaseGates: runs against every gate's citations — blocks none of them
